         <div type="bio">
            <p>British writer and scholar of literature. After holding a professorship of rhetoric and English language at the University of Edinburgh for twenty years, he retired to Bath in 1915. Although Saintsbury’s <name type="work" key="ID_MISSING">A History of English Prose Rhythm</name> (London: Macmillan, 1912) was an important source for the “Oxen of the Sun” episode in <name type="work" key="ID_MISSING">Ulysses</name>, Joyce’s wish that Saintsbury would write a review of his book (<name type="work" key="ID_MISSING">LI</name> 195) was unfulfilled. <hi rend="bold">William Brockman</hi>
                </p>
         </div>
